<%# Turn posted: append the new turn to the pinned transcript, then replace the
    composer (now "waiting for @opponent" for the mover). The pinned dom_ids let
    Increment 2b broadcasting drop in untouched. %>
<%= turbo_stream.append dom_id(@debate, :transcript) do %>
  <%= render "debates/debate_turn", debate_turn: @turn, debate: @debate %>
<% end %>
<%= turbo_stream.replace dom_id(@debate, :composer) do %>
  <%= render "debates/turn_composer", debate: @debate %>
<% end %>
<%# Slice 9: the turn also moved the round counter and may have opened the Extend
    window, so both regions have to be repainted for the MOVER too.

    Synchronously, and not only via post_turn's broadcast_state_change, because every
    *_later_to renders in a job — and in dev there is no worker, so that broadcast
    never lands (the Slice 8 review catch, same as extend_rounds.turbo_stream.erb).
    The async broadcast targets these same dom_ids, so when a worker IS running the
    second replace is an idempotent no-op.

    `viewer:` is passed EXPLICITLY: _debate_actions falls back to current_user only
    for the request context, and it must render for the actor here, not blank. %>
<%= turbo_stream.replace dom_id(@debate, :status) do %>
  <%= render "debates/debate_status", debate: @debate %>
<% end %>
<%= turbo_stream.replace dom_id(@debate, :actions) do %>
  <%= render "debates/debate_actions", debate: @debate, viewer: current_user %>
<% end %>
